<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammad Daoud Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammad Daoud Khan was an Afghan prince and politician who served as prime minister under his cousin King Zahir Shah from 1953 to 1963. In 1973 he overthrew the monarchy and founded the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, ruling as its president. He was killed with most of his family in the communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saur-revolution">Saur Revolution</a> of April 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohammad-daoud-khan.jpg" alt="Mohammad Daoud Khan" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author / Government of Afghanistan; processing by Roman Kubanskiy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mohammad_Daoud_Khan_official_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
